{"tool_name":"cidre","contents":["neubias"],"fetched_metadata":{"neubias":{"body":[{"format":"basic_html","processed":"<p>CIDRE is a retrospective illumination correction method for optical microscopy. It is designed to correct collections of images by building a model of the illumination distortion directly from the image data. Larger image collections provide more robust corrections. Details of the method are described in</p>\n\n<p>K. Smith, Y. Li, F. Ficcinini, G. Csucs, A. Bevilacqua, and P. Horvath<br>\nCIDRE: An Illumination Correction Method for Optical Microscopy, Nature Methods 12(5), 2015, doi:10.1038/NMETH.3323</p>","summary":"","value":"<p>CIDRE is a retrospective illumination correction method for optical microscopy. It is designed to correct collections of images by building a model of the illumination distortion directly from the image data. Larger image collections provide more robust corrections. Details of the method are described in</p>\r\n\r\n<p>K. Smith, Y. Li, F. Ficcinini, G. Csucs, A. Bevilacqua, and P. Horvath<br />\r\nCIDRE: An Illumination Correction Method for Optical Microscopy, Nature Methods 12(5), 2015, doi:10.1038/NMETH.3323</p>\r\n"}],"changed":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2023-04-29T12:27:21+00:00"}],"created":[{"format":"Y-m-d\\TH:i:sP","value":"2017-09-12T07:53:59+00:00"}],"default_langcode":[{"value":true}],"attribution_instructions":[],"comments_2023":[],"free_tagging":[],"give_feedback_on_this_soft":[{"cid":0,"comment_count":0,"last_comment_name":null,"last_comment_timestamp":1505203927,"last_comment_uid":41,"status":2}],"has_author":[{"value":"Kevin Smith"}],"has_biological_terms":[],"has_comparison":[{"options":[],"title":"","uri":"http://www.nature.com/nmeth/journal/v12/n5/full/nmeth.3323.html"}],"has_documentation":[],"has_doi":[{"options":[],"title":"10.1038/nmeth.3323","uri":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.3323"}],"has_entry_curator":[{"target_id":19,"target_type":"user","target_uuid":"a8a58b02-2abc-4749-8aea-b9